{
  "body" : "You are designing an elegant ukiyo-e inspired illustration, capturing the timeless beauty of traditional Japanese aesthetics.\n\nCONTENT BRIEF\n- Character depiction: {{character}}\n- Setting or backdrop: {{setting}}\n\nSTYLE DIRECTION\n- Genre / medium: Traditional Japanese ukiyo-e style illustration\n- Composition: Vertical orientation (3:2 portrait), using off-center framing with the main subject occupying the middle-right section, complemented by balanced negative space\n- Lens / camera: Flattened perspective with no depth exaggeration, evoking a hand-drawn two-dimensional character\n- Lighting: Soft, diffuse lighting with no distinct source to maintain a timeless and serene ambiance\n- Color palette and grading: Muted tones dominated by indigos, creams, and soft pinks, with gold accents for subtle contrast\n- Texture / surface: Aged paper texture with fine grain, emulating traditional woodblock prints\n- Post-processing: Subtle ink-line detailing with clean yet organic strokes\n- Mood: Graceful, tranquil, refined, nostalgic\n- References: Traditional ukiyo-e prints, Japanese cherry blossom motifs, intricate kimono patterns\n\nDESIGN RULES\n- Aspect: 3:2 portrait (~1024×1536) suitable for vertical displays\n- Maintain the delicacy of line work and color blending typical of ukiyo-e prints\n- Ensure balanced negative space to highlight the elegance of the composition\n\nAVOID\n- No overly modern or synthetic elements\n- No harsh lighting or shadows\n- No overly saturated or neon colors\n- No cluttered backgrounds that compete with the subject\n- No disproportionate or exaggerated anatomy\n- No absence of texture that emulates traditional woodblock prints\n\nAdditional constraints: {{extra}}\n\n——————\nCharacter: {{character}}\nSetting: {{setting}}\nExtra notes: {{extra}}",
